    "gold_solution": "```python\nfrom gurobipy import *\n\ndef solve_problem():\n    m = Model(\"Transportation_Problem\")\n    m.setParam(\"TimeLimit\", 100)  # Set time limit to 100 seconds\n\n    # Data\n    sources = list(range(20))  # S0..S19\n    destinations = list(range(3))  # D0..D2\n\n    supplies = [38, 51, 24, 39, 25, 66, 50, 29, 35, 24, 25, 37, 68, 57, 28, 52, 32, 42, 22, 68]\n    demands = [58, 31, 41]\n\n    # Cost matrix: rows correspond to sources S0..S19, columns to destinations D0..D2\n    costs = [\n        [  9.71,  12.53,  28.39],  # S0\n        [ 12.04,   8.37,  12.88],  # S1\n        [ 19.06,  12.70,  27.84],  # S2\n        [ 29.13,   6.50,  26.44],  # S3\n        [ 16.41,  26.78,  24.46],  # S4\n        [ 23.18,   7.39,  14.98],  # S5\n        [  9.85,  10.61,   5.35],  # S6\n        [ 10.16,   9.72,  16.47],  # S7\n        [ 10.82,   9.95,   8.02],  # S8\n        [ 22.64,  22.33,  17.06],  # S9\n        [ 26.63,  18.02,  21.84],  # S10\n        [ 10.67,   5.14,  13.31],  # S11\n        [ 29.46,   7.01,   9.43],  # S12\n        [ 27.64,  14.77,   5.63],  # S13\n        [ 14.16,  14.70,  22.19],  # S14\n        [ 14.38,   8.79,   8.17],  # S15\n        [ 23.88,  12.12,  24.30],  # S16\n        [ 23.91,  28.63,  26.34],  # S17\n        [ 11.22,  10.65,  24.87],  # S18\n        [ 26.08,  18.74,   8.99],  # S19\n    ]\n\n    # Decision variables:\n    # Flow_S{i}_D{j} >= 0 is the quantity shipped from source i to destination j\n    flows = {}\n    for i in sources:\n        for j in destinations:\n            flows[(i, j)] = m.addVar(lb=0.0, vtype=GRB.INTEGER, name=f\"Flow_S{i}_D{j}\")\n\n    # Objective: Minimize total transportation cost\n    m.setObjective(\n        quicksum(costs[i][j] * flows[(i, j)] for i in sources for j in destinations),\n        GRB.MINIMIZE\n    )\n\n    # Supply constraints: Shipments from each source <= its supply\n    for i in sources:\n        m.addConstr(\n            quicksum(flows[(i, j)] for j in destinations) <= supplies[i],\n            name=f\"Supply_S{i}\"\n        )\n\n    # Demand constraints: Shipments to each destination >= its demand\n    for j in destinations:\n        m.addConstr(\n            quicksum(flows[(i, j)] for i in sources) >= demands[j],\n            name=f\"Demand_D{j}\"\n        )\n\n    m.optimize()\n    return m\n```",
    "LLM_description": "Subject: Distribution plan to meet demand at lowest total shipping cost\nDate: [Insert Date]\nTo: [Executive Team]\nFrom: Supply Chain Director\n\nSituation:\nWe operate a network with multiple sources (warehouses, factories, and distribution centers) supplying several destinations (stores, customers, and regional hubs). Transportation spend is a major driver of overall cost, and delivery performance directly affects service levels and customer satisfaction. All moves must ship in whole unit quantities (no partial loads), which impacts how we consolidate and route shipments.\n\nProblem:\nWe need a practical shipping plan that assigns product from each source to each destination without exceeding available inventory at any source and fully meeting the required quantities at every destination. Shipping costs differ by route, so selecting the right lanes matters. The challenge is to coordinate inventory, capacity, and routing to cover demand at the lowest possible total shipping cost, while observing whole-unit requirements and our standard operating lead times. We will use the data in the annex to:\n- Confirm available inventory by source and required quantities by destination.\n- Compare lane costs to identify cost-effective routing options.\n- Build a source-to-destination allocation that ships in whole units, fulfills all orders, and avoids over-committing any location.\n- Highlight trade-offs (cost vs. service) and recommend actions for any bottlenecks (e.g., rebalancing inventory, adjusting pickup schedules, or sequencing shipments across periods).\n\nAnnex - Shipping Data:\n[38, 51, 24, 39, 25, 66, 50, 29, 35, 24, 25, 37, 68, 57, 28, 52, 32, 42, 22, 68]\n[58, 31, 41]\nCost Matrix (20 sources \u00d7 3 destinations):\n\nSource\\Dest | D 0 | D 1 | D 2\n-----------------------------\nS 0        |   9.71 |  12.53 |  28.39\nS 1        |  12.04 |   8.37 |  12.88\nS 2        |  19.06 |  12.70 |  27.84\nS 3        |  29.13 |   6.50 |  26.44\nS 4        |  16.41 |  26.78 |  24.46\nS 5        |  23.18 |   7.39 |  14.98\nS 6        |   9.85 |  10.61 |   5.35\nS 7        |  10.16 |   9.72 |  16.47\nS 8        |  10.82 |   9.95 |   8.02\nS 9        |  22.64 |  22.33 |  17.06\nS10        |  26.63 |  18.02 |  21.84\nS11        |  10.67 |   5.14 |  13.31\nS12        |  29.46 |   7.01 |   9.43\nS13        |  27.64 |  14.77 |   5.63\nS14        |  14.16 |  14.70 |  22.19\nS15        |  14.38 |   8.79 |   8.17\nS16        |  23.88 |  12.12 |  24.30\nS17        |  23.91 |  28.63 |  26.34\nS18        |  11.22 |  10.65 |  24.87\nS19        |  26.08 |  18.74 |   8.99",
    "LLM_description_template": "Subject: Cost-Effective Shipping Plan for Multi-Node Distribution\nDate: [Insert Date]\nFrom: Supply Chain Director\nTo: Leadership Team\n\nSituation:\nWe operate a network of warehouses and factories that must supply multiple store/customer locations. Freight rates vary across lanes, and inventories at each source are limited. To protect margins and uphold service commitments, we need a clear, efficient plan that directs shipments where they create the most value. All movements must be planned in whole units (no partial loads).\n\nProblem:\nWe need to allocate whole-unit shipments from each source to each destination in a way that:\n- Does not exceed available inventory at any source.\n- Fulfills the full requirement at every destination.\n- Lowers total transportation spend by prioritizing the most economical lanes.\n\nUsing our current source availability, destination needs, and lane-by-lane shipping costs, we will produce a load plan that assigns whole units across routes without breaching source limits and while fully covering destination demand. The result will be a practical, executable routing guide that balances cost and service, with clear load counts by source\u2013destination lane and an overall freight spend estimate.\n\nAnnex \u2013 Shipping Data:\n{SUPPLIES}\n{DEMANDS}\n{COST_MATRIX}"
